{
  "title": "Boss: the order book",
  "summary": "Load, inspect, select, derive and rank a shop's orders.",
  "minutes": 15,
  "kind": "boss",
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "learn",
      "title": "The order book",
      "body": [
        "A small shop exports its orders as CSV text (columns `order_id`, `date`, `customer`,",
        "`product`, `qty`, `unit_price`). Each challenge adds a function; repeat the earlier ones in",
        "your answer when a later step builds on them (the starter has them). Every step's tests run",
        "on a fresh copy of the data. This is the export the tests use (the examples below call it `text`):",
        "",
        "```text",
        "order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price",
        "7,2024-03-04,Ana,Tea,2,4.50",
        "2,2024-03-01,Bo,Jam,3,8.00",
        "5,2024-03-03,Cy,Tea,3,0.99",
        "1,2024-03-01,Ana,Tea,2,4.50",
        "3,2024-03-02,Di,Mug,1,8.00",
        "8,2024-03-05,Ana,Jam,5,3.50",
        "6,2024-03-03,Bo,Mug,10,4.00",
        "4,2024-03-02,Cy,Tea,1,4.50",
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Load the orders",
      "prompt": [
        "Write `load_orders(text)` that reads the CSV text and returns a DataFrame:",
        "",
        "- indexed by `order_id`,",
        "- with a new column `total` = `qty * unit_price`, rounded to 2 decimals,",
        "- sorted by `order_id`.",
        "",
        "```text",
        "order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price",
        "7,2024-03-02,Ana,Tea,2,4.50",
        "3,2024-03-01,Bo,Mug,1,8.00",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import io\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef load_orders(text):\n    pass\n",
      "solution": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def load_orders(text):",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")",
        "    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "    return df.sort_index()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")`",
        "Add `total`, then `return df.sort_index()`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "_ORDERS = 'order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price\\n7,2024-03-04,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n2,2024-03-01,Bo,Jam,3,8.00\\n5,2024-03-03,Cy,Tea,3,0.99\\n1,2024-03-01,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n3,2024-03-02,Di,Mug,1,8.00\\n8,2024-03-05,Ana,Jam,5,3.50\\n6,2024-03-03,Bo,Mug,10,4.00\\n4,2024-03-02,Cy,Tea,1,4.50\\n'",
        "_df = load_orders(_ORDERS)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"indexed and sorted by order_id\", [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], _df.index.tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"columns\", [\"date\", \"customer\", \"product\", \"qty\", \"unit_price\", \"total\"], list(_df.columns))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"totals\", [9.0, 24.0, 8.0, 4.5, 2.97, 40.0, 9.0, 17.5], _df[\"total\"].tolist())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Big orders",
      "prompt": [
        "Add `big_orders(df, min_total)`: a plain list of the order ids whose `total` is at least",
        "`min_total`, **largest total first** (ties: smaller order id first).",
        "",
        "```python",
        "big_orders(load_orders(text), 10)   # [6, 2, 8]",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import io\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef load_orders(text):\n    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")\n    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)\n    return df.sort_index()\n",
      "solution": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def load_orders(text):",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")",
        "    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "    return df.sort_index()",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "def big_orders(df, min_total):",
        "    big = df[df[\"total\"] >= min_total]",
        "    return big.sort_values(\"total\", ascending=False, kind=\"stable\").index.tolist()"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Filter with `df[df[\"total\"] >= min_total]`.",
        "`sort_values(\"total\", ascending=False, kind=\"stable\")` keeps id order for ties (the frame is already sorted by id)."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "_ORDERS = 'order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price\\n7,2024-03-04,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n2,2024-03-01,Bo,Jam,3,8.00\\n5,2024-03-03,Cy,Tea,3,0.99\\n1,2024-03-01,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n3,2024-03-02,Di,Mug,1,8.00\\n8,2024-03-05,Ana,Jam,5,3.50\\n6,2024-03-03,Bo,Mug,10,4.00\\n4,2024-03-02,Cy,Tea,1,4.50\\n'",
        "_df = load_orders(_ORDERS)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"at least 10\", [6, 2, 8], list(big_orders(_df, 10)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"at least 9 (ties by id)\", [6, 2, 8, 1, 7], list(big_orders(_df, 9)))",
        "Dojo.eq(\"none\", [], list(big_orders(_df, 1000)))"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Customer summary",
      "prompt": [
        "Add `customer_summary(df)` returning a dict with:",
        "",
        "- `\"customers\"`: number of distinct customers (`int`),",
        "- `\"top_customer\"`: the customer with the **most orders** (ties: alphabetical first),",
        "- `\"tea_share\"`: the percentage of orders that are for `Tea`, rounded to 1 decimal,",
        "- `\"biggest_qty\"`: the `product` of the single order with the largest `qty`.",
        "",
        "Use `nunique`, `value_counts` and `idxmax` (which returns the **index label** of the",
        "maximum, here an order id).",
        "",
        "```python",
        "customer_summary(load_orders(text))",
        "# {\"customers\": 4, \"top_customer\": \"Ana\", \"tea_share\": 50.0, \"biggest_qty\": \"Mug\"}",
        "```"
      ],
      "starter": "import io\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef load_orders(text):\n    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")\n    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)\n    return df.sort_index()\n",
      "solution": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def load_orders(text):",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")",
        "    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "    return df.sort_index()",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "def customer_summary(df):",
        "    counts = df[\"customer\"].value_counts()",
        "    top = sorted(counts[counts == counts.max()].index)[0]",
        "    return {",
        "        \"customers\": int(df[\"customer\"].nunique()),",
        "        \"top_customer\": top,",
        "        \"tea_share\": round(float((df[\"product\"] == \"Tea\").mean() * 100), 1),",
        "        \"biggest_qty\": df.loc[df[\"qty\"].idxmax(), \"product\"],",
        "    }"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "`counts = df[\"customer\"].value_counts()`; the tied leaders are `counts[counts == counts.max()].index`.",
        "`(df[\"product\"] == \"Tea\").mean()` is a fraction; `df.loc[df[\"qty\"].idxmax(), \"product\"]`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "_ORDERS = 'order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price\\n7,2024-03-04,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n2,2024-03-01,Bo,Jam,3,8.00\\n5,2024-03-03,Cy,Tea,3,0.99\\n1,2024-03-01,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n3,2024-03-02,Di,Mug,1,8.00\\n8,2024-03-05,Ana,Jam,5,3.50\\n6,2024-03-03,Bo,Mug,10,4.00\\n4,2024-03-02,Cy,Tea,1,4.50\\n'",
        "_df = load_orders(_ORDERS)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"summary\", {\"customers\": 4, \"top_customer\": \"Ana\", \"tea_share\": 50.0, \"biggest_qty\": \"Mug\"}, customer_summary(_df))",
        "_small = _df.loc[[2, 5]]",
        "Dojo.eq(\"tie on orders goes alphabetical\", {\"customers\": 2, \"top_customer\": \"Bo\", \"tea_share\": 50.0, \"biggest_qty\": \"Jam\"}, customer_summary(_small))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "title": "Fix the bad rows",
      "prompt": [
        "Some exported orders have a **negative** `qty` (returns entered wrongly). Add",
        "`fix_negatives(df)` that returns a **new** DataFrame where:",
        "",
        "- a `flagged` column is `True` for rows whose `qty` was negative, else `False`,",
        "- those rows' `qty` is made positive (`abs`),",
        "- `total` is recomputed for **every** row (`qty * unit_price`, rounded to 2 decimals).",
        "",
        "The DataFrame passed in must not change."
      ],
      "starter": "import io\nimport pandas as pd\n\n\ndef load_orders(text):\n    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")\n    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)\n    return df.sort_index()\n",
      "solution": [
        "import io",
        "import pandas as pd",
        "",
        "",
        "def load_orders(text):",
        "    df = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(text), index_col=\"order_id\")",
        "    df[\"total\"] = (df[\"qty\"] * df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "    return df.sort_index()",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "",
        "def fix_negatives(df):",
        "    out = df.copy()",
        "    out[\"flagged\"] = out[\"qty\"] < 0",
        "    out.loc[out[\"flagged\"], \"qty\"] = out.loc[out[\"flagged\"], \"qty\"].abs()",
        "    out[\"total\"] = (out[\"qty\"] * out[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "    return out"
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Start with `out = df.copy()` and `out[\"flagged\"] = out[\"qty\"] < 0`.",
        "`out.loc[out[\"flagged\"], \"qty\"] = out.loc[out[\"flagged\"], \"qty\"].abs()`, then recompute `total`."
      ],
      "template": [
        "{{CODE}}",
        "_ORDERS = 'order_id,date,customer,product,qty,unit_price\\n7,2024-03-04,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n2,2024-03-01,Bo,Jam,3,8.00\\n5,2024-03-03,Cy,Tea,3,0.99\\n1,2024-03-01,Ana,Tea,2,4.50\\n3,2024-03-02,Di,Mug,1,8.00\\n8,2024-03-05,Ana,Jam,5,3.50\\n6,2024-03-03,Bo,Mug,10,4.00\\n4,2024-03-02,Cy,Tea,1,4.50\\n'",
        "_df = load_orders(_ORDERS)",
        "_df.loc[3, \"qty\"] = -1",
        "_df.loc[8, \"qty\"] = -5",
        "_df[\"total\"] = (_df[\"qty\"] * _df[\"unit_price\"]).round(2)",
        "_out = fix_negatives(_df)",
        "Dojo.eq(\"flagged\", [False, False, True, False, False, False, False, True], [bool(v) for v in _out[\"flagged\"].tolist()])",
        "Dojo.eq(\"qty made positive\", [2, 3, 1, 1, 3, 10, 2, 5], _out[\"qty\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"totals recomputed\", [9.0, 24.0, 8.0, 4.5, 2.97, 40.0, 9.0, 17.5], _out[\"total\"].tolist())",
        "Dojo.eq(\"the input is unchanged\", [-1, -5], [int(_df.loc[3, \"qty\"]), int(_df.loc[8, \"qty\"])])"
      ],
      "forbid": [
        {
          "pattern": "\\bfor\\b",
          "message": "No loop"
        },
        {
          "pattern": "\\]\\s*\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\s*=[^=]",
          "message": "No chained assignment"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
